#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Safely preview, interactively select, and clean orphaned Antigravity sessions
left behind by T3 Code on macOS.

Design invariants (fail-closed):
  1. Never clean if a newer T3 state DB (e.g. statev3.sqlite) exists or expected
     SQLite tables/columns are missing.
  2. Never clean if live Antigravity threads exist in T3 yet 0 disk sessions match
     the parsed active whitelist (guards against T3 schema/format drift).
  3. Wide whitelist (live + archived threads, nested native subagents, pending
     handoffs/transfers/outbox, open lsof handles, cooldown window) + narrow
     evidence-based deletion.
  4. Real-time re-verification right before touching disk (prevents TOCTOU races).
  5. Default CLI cleanup is pure file-only bundled Trash (manifest.json +
     restore.sh); conversation_summaries.db is only mutated when requested
     (--prune-summaries in CLI, or synced in TUI when T3 is completely closed,
     with per-run toggle) after schema verification and a consistent WAL-merged
     snapshot backup in Trash.
"""

